{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"The RNG mismatch is loader interposition, not algorithmic: both drivers already produce the same KAT digest in separate processes, but loading two libraries that export `DRBG_ctx` into one global namespace causes the second library’s internal references to bind to the first library’s state. I’m isolating the Rust library with deep binding so each implementation uses its own exported global, which is required for a valid in-process differential test."}}
