{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"agent_message","text":"The heap corruption is another C-specific shape: BLAKE `gen_message_random` calls `blake*_final` directly into `R`; for the 128-bit sets C writes a full 32-byte BLAKE-256 digest even though callers consume only the first 16 bytes. The production signature buffer has room, but my standalone test allocated only 16. I’m reproducing the actual caller-sized backing storage and comparing the consumed `SPX_N` bytes."}}
