{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"agent_message","text":"The direct FORS leaf output matches, but its state side effect does not: C mutates `fors_gen_leaf_info.leaf_addrx`; Rust operated on a copy and discarded the updated address. That mutation feeds the treehash traversal state and explains the composed FORS divergence. I’m fixing the Rust implementation to write the final leaf address back exactly as C does."}}
