{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"agent_message","text":"The remaining FORS mismatch comes from a broader address-translation incompleteness exposed by randomized raw addresses: C always writes and copies the full four-byte keypair field, while Rust only handled the low one or two bytes based on tree height. Real generated indices often hide this because upper bytes are zero. I’m changing both keypair address operations to the exact four-byte C behavior."}}
