{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_132","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' ERRORS.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Error-surface table\n\nMechanically derived from explicit rejection returns, null checks, abort paths,\nand driver failure returns in `app/` and `lib/`. Pointer-taking APIs not listed\nbelow contain no C null check; passing null where storage is dereferenced is C\nundefined behavior rather than a library rejection.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 1 | `seedexpander_init` | `maxlen >= 0x100000000` | `RNG_BAD_MAXLEN` (`-1`) |\n| 2 | `seedexpander` | output pointer `x == NULL` | `RNG_BAD_OUTBUF` (`-2`) |\n| 3 | `seedexpander` | `xlen >= ctx->length_remaining` (including equality) | `RNG_BAD_REQ_LEN` (`-3`) |\n| 4 | `crypto_sign_verify` | `siglen != SPX_BYTES` (zero, one short, or one long included) | `-1` |\n| 5 | `crypto_sign_verify` | reconstructed root differs from `pk + SPX_N` | `-1` |\n| 6 | `crypto_sign_open` | `smlen < SPX_BYTES` | zero `m[0..smlen]`, set `*mlen = 0`, return `-1` |\n| 7 | `crypto_sign_open` | detached verification of the signed-message prefix fails | zero `m[0..smlen]`, set `*mlen = 0`, return `-1` |\n| 8 | `AES256_ECB` | `EVP_CIPHER_CTX_new()` fails | print OpenSSL errors and `abort()` |\n| 9 | `AES256_ECB` | `EVP_EncryptInit_ex(...) != 1` | print OpenSSL errors and `abort()` |\n| 10 | `AES256_ECB` | `EVP_EncryptUpdate(...) != 1` | print OpenSSL errors and `abort()` |\n| 11 | C driver `main` | generated `mlen > BASE_MLEN * LOOP_COUNT` | print `mlen overflow`, return `KAT_OVERFLOW` |\n| 12 | C driver `main` | `crypto_sign_keypair` returns nonzero | print function result, return `KAT_CRYPTO_FAILURE` |\n| 13 | C driver `main` | `crypto_sign` returns nonzero | print function result, return `KAT_CRYPTO_FAILURE` |\n| 14 | C driver `main` | `crypto_sign_open` returns nonzero | print function result, return `KAT_CRYPTO_FAILURE` |\n| 15 | C driver `main` | opened length differs from original length | print `mlen mismatch`, return `KAT_CRYPTO_FAILURE` |\n| 16 | C driver `main` | opened bytes differ from original message | print `m mismatch`, return `KAT_CRYPTO_FAILURE` |\n\nNo public C API uses an enum type. Address type is a raw `uint32_t`; all\nvalues, including values outside `0..=6`, are accepted and encoded without an\nerror return.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
